From 47ad04fd8a0977e3fecc475f097d2e2be5e1b80b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noah Cylich <noahcylich@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:06:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] temporal-MoE CUDA: TEMPORAL_FUSED_ADD, residual add in the
 fused op; TEMPORAL_QKV=2, attention norm in the launch that quantises the
 Q/K/V input

TEMPORAL_FUSED_ADD=1: the ADD of the residual stream that follows the fused MoE op is done by the op's
down launch (one float add per element, same operands) when it is the next node and the op's only consumer.

TEMPORAL_QKV=2: as 1, and the RMS norm and weight that produce the projections' input are computed by the
launch that quantises it (rms_norm_mul_q8_1: the sum of squares is reduced as rms_norm_f32 reduces it, the
quantisation is quantize_q8_1's).

TEMPORAL_GRAPHDUMP=n (debugging): print the first n nodes of the first single-token graph.

All off by default.
